# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: ntruhrss-r1-pack-tail-in-bounds
why: poly_S3_tobytes / poly_S3_frombytes pack NTRU_PACK_DEG = 700 trits five per byte into
why: NTRU_OWCPA_MSGBYTES = (700+4)/5 = 140 bytes, then handle a partial last byte at index 700/5 = 140
why: that does not exist when 5 divides 700: tobytes writes msg[140] and frombytes reads msg[140], one
why: byte past the buffer (the 140-byte stack array m in ntrukem.c; macOS's stack protector aborts,
why: CI run 45513495947). The round 2 package fixes it with `#if NTRU_PACK_DEG > (NTRU_PACK_DEG / 5) * 5`.
why: The patch starts the tail at the last full byte (139) when 5 divides 700: tobytes recomputes
why: msg[139] from the same five coefficients, frombytes recomputes coeffs 695..699 from msg[139]
why: (c*171>>9 repeated equals the direct c*57>>9, c*19>>9, c*203>>14 for every byte value), so the
why: output is identical and nothing outside the buffers is touched.
file: upstream/crypto_kem/ntruhrss701/poly.c
count: 2
find:   i = NTRU_PACK_DEG/5;
replace:   i = NTRU_PACK_DEG/5 - (NTRU_PACK_DEG % 5 == 0);
